# Claude Code local configuration.
#
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/`, because git does not descend into an
# excluded DIRECTORY — with a trailing slash, no `!` rule underneath can ever
# re-include anything. The two-step dance below is the only way to publish one
# subdirectory out of an otherwise-ignored tree.
#
# settings.local.json stays ignored: it is per-machine configuration.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*

# Tracked ON PURPOSE: git-guard is the workflow every contributor is supposed
# to run before committing, and a rule that lives only on one laptop is not a
# rule. It has to sit here rather than in docs/ — Claude Code only discovers
# skills under `.claude/skills/`, so moving the file would stop it being
# invokable, which is the whole point of it.
#
# The other three skills (plan-week, work-week, feature-research) are still
# local. They are RIVR-specific too, so tracking them is a reasonable next
# step, but that publishes Jerson's working process to the repo and is his
# call rather than a side effect of this one.
!.claude/skills/git-guard/

# Internal team docs (local-only, never commit)
docs/internal/
functions_geoglows/.env
